policy timeout \\\n      --hicache-io-backend kernel --hicache-mem-layout page_first \\\n      --page-size 64\n\nthe server hits a Segmentation fault on both TP ranks during the first device→host KV backup (the first L3 write_through backup after serving starts):\n    \n    `Segmentation fault\n      ... HiCacheStagedWriteBackKernel ...\n      ... cuMemcpyBatchAsync ...\n    `\n\n(full backtrace in the comments)\n\n## Root cause analysis\n\nThe JIT kvcacheio path resolves the batched-memcpy entry point at runtime via `dlsym`, but selects the function-pointer signature (ABI) at compile time:\n\n`python/sglang/kernels/jit/csrc/kvcacheio/staged_write_back.cuh` (as shipped in 0.5.18):\n    \n    #if !defined(USE_ROCM) && defined(CUDA_VERSION) && CUDA_VERSION >= 12080\n    #if CUDA_VERSION >= 13000   // <-- compile-time: the local nvcc's headers decide the ABI\n    using CudaMemcpyBatchAsyncFn = cudaError_t (*)(\n        const void*, const void*, const size_t*, size_t,\n        cudaMemcpyAttributes*, size_t*, size_t, cudaStream_t);   // 8 args, CUDA 13\n    #else\n    using CudaMemcpyBatchAsyncFn = cudaError_t (*)(\n        void**, void**, size_t*, size_t,\n        cudaMemcpyAttributes*, size_t*, size_t, size_t*, cudaStream_t); // 9 args, CUDA 12.8 (failIdx)\n    #endif\n    \n    inline auto get_cuda_memcpy_batch_async() -> CudaMemcpyBatchAsyncFn {\n      static CudaMemcpyBatchAsyncFn cuda_memcpy_batch_async = []() {\n        void* symbol = dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, \"cudaMemcpyBatchAsync\"); // <-- runtime: loaded libcudart decides\n        return reinterpret_cast<CudaMemcpyBatchAsyncFn>(symbol);\n      }();\n      return cuda_memcpy_batch_async;\n    }\n\nCUDA 13 removed the `failIdx` argument from `cudaMemcpyBatchAsync` (9 args in CUDA 12.8, 8 args in 13.0). When the two sources of truth disagree, the call segfaults (no `cudaError_t` is returned; the existing error check + `copy_page_first_pages_fallback` at lines 177–181 is never reached).\n\nOur host is a very common dual-toolchain setup:\n\nComponent  | Version\n--- | ---\n`nvcc` used by the JIT (`/usr/local/cuda` → 12.8)  | CUDA 12.8.93\n`libcudart` loaded by the process (torch `2.13.0+cu130`)  | CUDA 13.0.3\n\nThe JIT object was compiled with 12.8 headers — proven by the build dependency file in the JIT cache (`/root/.cache/sglang/jit/sm86/sgl_kernel_jit_hicache_staged_512_4_2_1024/build-*/deps-*/cuda_0.o.d`), which lists:\n    \n    `/usr/local/cuda-12.8/bin/../targets/x86_64-linux/include/cuda_runtime.h\n    `\n\nSo: compile-time `CUDA_VERSION = 12080` → 9-arg ABI selected → `dlsym` resolves the 8-arg CUDA 13.0 `cudaMemcpyBatchAsync` → first `try_copy_page_first_pages_batch` call segfaults.\n\nThe mirror-image configuration (JIT compiled with 13.x headers, process running on a 12.8 runtime) would break the same way.\n\nThis is the same class of bug as #21869 (\"CUDA 13 removed `failIdx` from batched memcpy APIs\"), which was fixed only in the AOT path (`sgl-kernel/csrc/kvcacheio/transfer.cu`, PRs #23136 / #23172 / #23183). The JIT path carries the same pattern in `staged_write_back.cuh`. vLLM and lmdeploy hit the identical ABI break and fixed it with runtime entry-point dispatch (vLLM #44784 — \"Prevent cuMemcpyBatchAsync segfault with MTP and KV offloading\"; InternLM/lmdeploy #4838 — \"CUDA 13 removed failIdx from batched memcpy APIs, so calling the v12080 entry point on cu13 builds segfaults. Select the matching driver entry point at runtime\").\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFix CUDA 13 cudaMemcpyBatchAsync segfault and restore hicache CI · sgl-project/sglang@4bb88a4 · GitHub (https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/24685446696)\nciteturn6search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 4 weeks ago; # Fix CUDA 13 cudaMemcpyBatchAsync segfault and restore hicache CI #9886\n\n# Fix CUDA 13 cudaMemcpyBatchAsync segfault and restore hicache CI #9886\n\n  * Sign in to view logs\n\n## Summary\n\n# Fix CUDA 13 cudaMemcpyBatchAsync segfault and restore hicache CI\n\n## \n\nFix CUDA 13 cudaMemcpyBatchAsync segfault and restore hicache CI #9886\n\n\nTriggered via pull request April 20, 2026 19:14\n\nKangyan-Zhou\n\nclosed #23183\n\nStatus Skipped\n\nTotal duration 1s\n\nArtifacts –\n\n## cancel-pr-workflow-on-merge.yml\n\non: pull_request_target\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n⚙️ AI Infrastructure Digest 2026-08-26 · Issue #2922 · duanyytop/agents-radar · GitHub (https://github.com/duanyytop/agents-radar/issues/2922)\nciteturn6search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: today;   * HiCache L3 segfault on first backup: Issue #36302 is a JIT ABI mismatch in `staged_write_back.cuh` between nvcc 12.8 co